IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`
IMPORT `roc5-o20`

-- TESTS for roc5-o20.l4 (Order 20, rules 1 to 7).  Every expected value is written from the text of the
-- Rules (lines 2876 to 2904 of the raw file), beside the assertion, before the module was run.
-- A "last day" below is a made-up answer of O 3 r 3 (seam S-T1): 15 March 2027 stands for "14 days after
-- the tribunal's decision of 1 March 2027", and so on.

§ `Tests -- Order 20`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- scope`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1)(a): an appeal against a tribunal's decision, provided for by written law, not from a State Court,
-- and Order 19, Rule 41 says nothing special: the Order applies.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 20 r 1(1)(a) an appeal against the decision of a tribunal` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(a) "except as otherwise provided in Order 19, Rule 41": that Rule provides for the appeal: no.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 20 r 1(1)(a) an appeal against the decision of a tribunal` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Whether Order 19, Rule 41 provides for it is that Rule's answer: not known, not covered.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 20 r 1(1)(a) an appeal against the decision of a tribunal` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(b): an application for a case stated is not subject to the Rule 41 exception (the parenthesis is in (a)).
#ASSERT `o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 20 r 1(1)(b) an application for a case to be stated or an application by way of case stated to the General Division` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "where such an appeal or application is provided by the written law": it is not: no.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 20 r 1(1)(a) an appeal against the decision of a tribunal` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 20 r 1(1)(b) an application for a case to be stated or an application by way of case stated to the General Division` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): an appeal from a State Court constituted under the State Courts Act: the Order does not apply.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 20 r 1(1)(a) an appeal against the decision of a tribunal` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A proceeding of another kind is outside the scope (no "only"): not covered.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 20 r 1(1) another kind of proceeding` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- definitions`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "record of proceedings" means each listed kind of document in respect of the proceedings before the tribunal.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 20 r 2 written grounds of decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 20 r 2 record of evidence or notes of arguments taken` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 20 r 2 affidavit or statutory declaration filed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 20 r 2 submissions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 20 r 2 any other document tendered` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not in respect of the tribunal's proceedings: "means ... in respect of the proceedings before the tribunal": no.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 20 r 2 submissions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 20 r 2 any other document tendered` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "tribunal" includes any authority, person or body authorised under any written law, but not any Court.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a body is a tribunal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a body is a tribunal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a body is a tribunal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither authorised under a written law nor a Court: "includes", the list is not closed: not covered.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 2 a body is a tribunal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- bringing of the appeal or application`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): by originating application supported by an affidavit.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(1) the appeal or application is brought in the way the rule requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(1) the appeal or application is brought in the way the rule requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(1) the appeal or application is brought in the way the rule requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2): 14 days after the tribunal's decision of 1 March 2027 ends on 15 March 2027 (made-up O 3 r 3 answer).
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(2) the period for filing and serving the originating application and the supporting affidavit`'s `period length` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(2) the period for filing and serving the originating application and the supporting affidavit`'s `period unit` EQUALS Days
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are filed and served in time` (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are filed and served in time` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 10 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one day late, filing or service: no.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are filed and served in time` (Date 16 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are filed and served in time` (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 16 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- served on all parties who have an interest in the matter.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are served on every interested party` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are served on every interested party` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (3): the affidavit states the facts, the questions and the orders sought.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(3) the affidavit states what the rule requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(3) the affidavit states what the rule requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(3) the affidavit states what the rule requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(3) the affidavit states what the rule requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (4): the record, "if that is available and is necessary".
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(4) the affidavit must include the record of proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(4) the affidavit must include the record of proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(4) the affidavit must include the record of proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (5): an affidavit in reply, if necessary, within 21 days after service.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(5) the period for the affidavit in reply`'s `period length` EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(5) a party served must file and serve an affidavit in reply` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(5) a party served must file and serve an affidavit in reply` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(5) a party served must file and serve an affidavit in reply` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- served on 15 March 2027: the 21st day is 5 April 2027 (made-up O 3 r 3 answer).
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(5) the affidavit in reply is filed and served in time` (Date 5 4 2027) (Date 5 4 2027) (Date 5 4 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(5) the affidavit in reply is filed and served in time` (Date 5 4 2027) (Date 6 4 2027) (Date 5 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 3(5) the affidavit in reply is filed and served in time` (Date 6 4 2027) (Date 5 4 2027) (Date 5 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- case conference`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ASSERT `o 20 r 4(1) the period for the case conference`'s `period length` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `o 20 r 4(1) the period for the case conference`'s `period unit` EQUALS Weeks
-- attended a case conference (O 9 r 1) on the last day of the 6 weeks: yes.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 4(1) the parties attend a case conference in time` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (Date 12 4 2027) (Date 12 4 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day after: no.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 4(1) the parties attend a case conference in time` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (Date 13 4 2027) (Date 12 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the parties did not attend: no.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 4(1) the parties attend a case conference in time` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 4 2027) (Date 12 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the meeting is not a case conference as O 9 r 1 describes: "means ... as described in Order 9, Rule 1": no (the keel's answer).
#ASSERT `o 20 r 4(1) the parties attend a case conference in time` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 4 2027) (Date 12 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Order 9, Rule 1's answer not known: not covered.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 4(1) the parties attend a case conference in time` TRUE NOTHING (Date 1 4 2027) (Date 12 4 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): at the case conference the Court must give directions.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 4(2) the Court must give the directions that are necessary` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 4(2) the Court must give the directions that are necessary` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 5 -- written submissions`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(1) the period for written submissions`'s `period length` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(1) the period for written submissions`'s `period direction` EQUALS `Before the anchor`
-- hearing on 30 March 2027: at least 14 days before is 16 March 2027 (made-up O 3 r 3 answer).
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(1) the written submissions are filed and served in time` (Date 16 3 2027) (Date 16 3 2027) (Date 16 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(1) the written submissions are filed and served in time` (Date 17 3 2027) (Date 16 3 2027) (Date 16 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(1) the written submissions are filed and served in time` (Date 16 3 2027) (Date 17 3 2027) (Date 16 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Subject to Rule 4": the case conference directions fix another time: not covered.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(1) the written submissions are filed and served in time` (Date 17 3 2027) (Date 17 3 2027) (Date 16 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(2) the page limit for each party or set of parties` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(2) the written submissions are within the page limit` 35 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(2) the written submissions are within the page limit` 36 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(2) the written submissions are within the page limit` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (3): special circumstances and the fees paid: yes; fees unpaid: no ("upon the payment"); no special circumstances: not covered.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(3) the Court may allow the page limit to be exceeded` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(3) the Court may allow the page limit to be exceeded` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(3) the Court may allow the page limit to be exceeded` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 5(3) the Court may allow the page limit to be exceeded` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 6 -- stay of enforcement`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "does not operate as a stay ... unless any written law otherwise provides or the Court otherwise orders".
#ASSERT `o 20 r 6 the appeal or application operates as a stay of enforcement of the tribunal's decision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 6 the appeal or application operates as a stay of enforcement of the tribunal's decision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 20 r 6 the appeal or application operates as a stay of enforcement of the tribunal's decision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 20 r 6 the appeal or application operates as a stay of enforcement of the tribunal's decision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 7 -- powers of the Court`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): the Court hearing the appeal has the powers Order 19, Rule 7 gives it.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 7(1) the Court hearing the appeal or application has the power` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Order 19, Rule 7 does not give this power: this rule says only that the Court has "the powers that the Court has under Order 19, Rule 7": not covered.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 7(1) the Court hearing the appeal or application has the power` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 20 r 7(1) the Court hearing the appeal or application has the power` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- not hearing an appeal or application under this Order: not covered.
#ASSERT `o 20 r 7(1) the Court hearing the appeal or application has the power` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): "If an appeal to the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal is permitted in the written law".
#ASSERT `o 20 r 7(2) the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal has the power` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 7(2) the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal has the power` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 20 r 7(2) the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal has the power` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
